{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/archive/component/aspace_4f72cead859351fef54aa9f46697b78f","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"aspace_4f72cead859351fef54aa9f46697b78f","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Bookkeeping, taxes, expenses","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"abstract","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/abstract"}],"content":"Seven sheets of records and notes found labeled, \"1946\". Eight sheets of records found concerning earth-moving labor and equipment, 1948-1950. Three sheets containing a check, a list of plants, and a lumber yard receipt, all dated 1950. Twenty-four sheets containing records and notes found labeled, \"1951\". Fourteen sheets containing records and notes found labeled, \"1952\"; with these is a letter from Maria Chabot to Mary Cabot Wheelwright, June 30, 1952, which details bills paid at Los Luceros. Six sheets of undated notes found scattered among the above files.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Related Material","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/relatedmaterial"}],"content":[],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Legal status statement","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/userestrict"}],"content":null,"type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}